course: dictionary
lesson: 9708
title: Sulphur: a yellow element with a strong smell
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sulphur is a noun. It is the name of a chemical element: a yellow solid that is not a metal. In America it is spelt «sulfur», but it means the same thing.
explain: The context gives you clues about its smell. «Rotten eggs smell because bacteria break down proteins with sulphur in them.» Sulphur is linked with a strong, rotten smell. Careful, though: the smell that people notice comes from a gas called hydrogen sulphide, not from the yellow solid itself.
explain: Context can also show you the colour. «Sulphur yellow is a bright pale yellow colour.» When you see sulphur used to describe a colour, ask: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Sulphur is a yellow chemical element, and its symbol is S.
fact: Sulphur is a solid that is not a metal.
fact: «Sulphur» burns with a blue flame.
fact: «Sulphur» is the British spelling; «sulfur» is the US spelling.
fact: Hydrogen sulphide is a gas that smells like rotten eggs; the yellow solid is a different thing.
exercise: What is sulphur? | A gas that smells sweet | A red metal that is easy to bend | A kind of cloud | *A yellow chemical element that is not a metal
exercise: «Rotten eggs smell because bacteria break down proteins with sulphur in them.» What gives off the smell of rotten eggs? | Sea water | Sugar going bad | Pure yellow sulphur solid | *A gas called hydrogen sulphide
exercise: Which spelling is used in America for the same element? | sulphur | sulphure | sulpur | *sulfur
test: «Sulphur burns with a blue flame.» What colour is the flame? | Red | Green | Yellow | *Blue
test: Which is the chemical symbol for sulphur? | Sh | Sf | *S | Su
exam: Which sentence about sulphur is true? | Sulphur is a soft silver metal | Sulphur is a liquid that is always blue | Sulphur is a gas that smells sweet | *Sulphur is a yellow solid that is not a metal
